WEBVTT

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.190
Here I come!

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:15.790
Princess is fast!

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:18.650
Princess's movements have grown more compact.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:19.660
Hmm.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.080
Yuu-kun, your turn!

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:28.340
Come at me whenever you're ready.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.460
Thank you!

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.130
I still don't quite get 
the point of the balloon.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.770
Sorry. I don't know, either.

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:50.480
I just tried it out on a whim.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.730
If we want to improve 
their chances of surviving,

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:58.180
shouldn't we have them practice dodging 
your attack like Yuuhi did before?

00:00:58.180 --> 00:00:59.330
That's true.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:01.520
Yuu-kun, trade off!

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:03.360
We're changing up the training!

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:04.480
Got it.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:09.160
Watch my attack closely and dodge it.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.750
Here I go.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.760
H-Hanako!

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:17.840
Oh, my.

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:21.850
Well, don't worry, 
I've never failed to stop short.

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:24.710
Not yet, at least.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:30.150
Hello?

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:31.750
<i>Oh, Yuu-kun?</i>

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:33.390
Yeah, what's up?

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:37.080
<i>Yuu-kun, what do you associate with summer?</i>

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:38.950
Can I hang up?

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:42.020
<i>Wha?! Yuu-kun, you meanie.</i>

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.230
Hurry up and state your business.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:47.500
When it comes to summer,

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:50.350
its beaches, swimsuits, and swimsuits!

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:52.800
Why did you mention swimsuits twice?

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:58.400
Which is why we're holding a summer 
training camp for the Beast Knights!

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.010
Training camp?

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:02.150
There.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:08.900
<i>Everyone was crying</i>

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:12.360
<i>Like a star burning blue</i>

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.740
<i>Where will we go? What will we see?</i>

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:20.540
<i>We're all going to change, though.</i>

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:37.960
<i>I don't need it, don't want it.</i>

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:40.070
<i>I've already given up on it</i>

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:41.730
<i>After so many sad farewells</i>

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:44.110
<i>And "take cares"</i>

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:49.430
<i>I want to like the present more than the past, 
the future more than the present.</i>

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:53.520
<i>Gradually my values have changed</i>

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.990
<i>I felt more grown up the more they wore away</i>

00:02:56.990 --> 00:03:02.880
<i>Lies and betrayals 
are practically civilities</i>

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:06.380
<i>Everyone ages</i>

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:09.830
<i>But what about the star burning blue?</i>

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:13.200
<i>Our likes and dislikes</i>

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:16.800
<i>They'll all change at some point</i>

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:19.670
<i>A worn-out savior</i>

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:21.350
<i>A medal in a dirty ditch</i>

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:25.180
<i>I don't want to overlook 
their faint glimmers of light</i>

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:28.980
<i>I hear the sound still ringing from them</i>

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:34.500
<i>Let's move on a bit</i>

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.270
Yahoo!

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:42.320
The beach!

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:43.520
Beach!

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:45.630
Swimsuits! Swimsuits!

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:48.120
<b>Episode 10: Hekatombaion and the Beast Knights</b>

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:48.620
There's no one here.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:52.020
Everyone else stays out the other way

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:54.330
since there's no vending machines 
or food stalls out here.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:57.710
It's the perfect secret spot for training.

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:59.400
Training?

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:02.490
No one's in the mood for that, Nagumocchi.

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:05.680
Hakudou-san, let's play!

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:08.740
Sorry, I'll be going.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:12.970
Shall we go do some fishing?

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:15.930
Yeah, that's fine.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.740
You backed down pretty easily.

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:25.110
Well, building teamwork 
is enough improvement on its own.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:30.050
It'll make it easier for us to coordinate 
when the seven-eyed one attacks.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:32.910
If we can also blow off steam, then great.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:37.170
I thought Nagumo-san was a stricter guy.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:38.710
That's how he really is.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.370
He's the one who brought the beach parasols.

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:46.640
<i>There are two types of people.</i>

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:49.470
<i>Those who can swim,</i>

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:52.210
<i>and those who can't.</i>

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.910
Hey! You three there!

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:56.860
Hanako!

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:58.900
I'll teach you how to swim, so come on!

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.360
People aren't designed to float that easily.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:03.440
No, they're not.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:04.980
Right?

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:07.990
Yuu-kun, come here!

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:07.990
Nice catch!

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.780
Princess, I'm coming!

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:19.870
Hey.

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:25.610
Let's have some drinks and guy talk.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:29.090
Huh? Where are the other guys?

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:32.560
Taiyou-kun's playing games 
on the sofa in the lobby.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:35.200
Shimaki-san and Nagumo-san are in the sauna.

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:37.670
Hmm.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:40.260
Well, guess we'll do it with just us.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:42.360
Though, you'll have something other than beer.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:44.500
What do you even mean by guy talk?

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:45.860
Are you already drunk?

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.440
What was that?

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:49.070
I can still drink more!

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:51.860
Well, whatever.

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:53.990
Now then...

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:55.680
Cheers!

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:08.560
Tarou-san, banquets require 
entertainment, right?

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:10.110
You got anything for us?

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:12.010
Some talent or trick?

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:14.440
It's not really a trick, but...

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:18.200
I can use this to...

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:28.510
Whoa!

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:30.450
You're incredibly skilled.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:36.210
It's something I thought up while 
I was working to be a chef.

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:39.520
It's kind of specialized 
into precision work.

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:46.500
Mikazuki-san, if you have 
some time, could you train me?

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:49.930
I feel like I still have a lot 
of room to improve on this,

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:53.070
and I'll probably get 
a hint during training.

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:55.760
Sure. Hana-chan, too?

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:56.880
If you could.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:01.350
Though, tell us, are you 
and Hana-chan dating?

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:04.320
We're not dating.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.110
Really?

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:07.900
We're just childhood friends!

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:08.840
You dummy!

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:12.200
Being childhood friends 
is nothing to scoff at!

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:16.030
They're neighbors and they can visit 
each other through their windows.

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:18.590
What the heck?!

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:19.960
So loud.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:23.780
Yuu-kun! Say something to 
this 80s romcom bastard!

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:25.510
Huh? Uh...

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:27.340
Inappropriate!

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:31.930
The Princess lives next to Yuuhi's room, 
so she often comes in through the window.

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:41.440
Yuu-kun, you Brutus!

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:44.940
<b>Et tu, Yuu-kun? Damn it!</b>

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:52.510
I'm going into the hot spring 
once more before bed.

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:53.990
Want to come with?

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:55.330
No.

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:58.570
I want to see the ocean at night, 
so I'm going for a walk.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:00.460
Roger that.

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:07.670
Cluck-cluck!

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:09.010
Ow!

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:11.170
Watch it, you damn nincompoop!

00:08:11.710 --> 00:08:12.800
Sorry, sorry!

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:13.810
Hmph!

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:17.060
You were shouting though, 
so what happened?

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:20.100
Oh, I just drank too much.

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:23.310
You're an adult, so please keep it together.

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:25.040
What?

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:28.750
If you want to lecture me, you're, uh,

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:29.780
two years too early!

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:32.210
Why two years?

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:35.420
I first fell in love in ninth grade!

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:37.430
Oh?

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:40.120
Did you fall for, um,

00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:43.080
s-someone younger?

00:08:43.430 --> 00:08:46.040
Yeah! She was younger.

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:48.180
O-Oh?

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:51.380
Did she go to the same school as you?

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:54.880
No. She was a four-year-old 
gold snubbed nose monkey.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.930
Gold Snubbed Nose Monkey

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:58.300
Are you drunk?

00:08:58.300 --> 00:08:59.210
Yeah.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:03.540
Get it together, please.

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:04.860
Shaddap.

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:19.230
Can you love the world?

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:26.520
A person?

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:27.730
Impossible.

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:29.130
They're walking on top of the ocean.

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:42.720
Oh, Yuu-kun!

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:45.350
P-Princess?!

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:47.810
Were you just walking on the water?

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:49.070
Yeah.

00:09:49.070 --> 00:09:51.270
I was practicing repelling water.

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:54.940
Though I'm wearing my swimsuit 
underneath in case I failed.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:58.410
What a wonderful combination!

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:02.990
Though, repelling water?

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:06.460
Well, I just had a feeling I could do it.

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:08.620
A feeling?

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:12.920
Lately, I've learned a bit about 
how to draw out my power.

00:10:13.390 --> 00:10:17.010
Seems like our superpowers 
are way more random

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:18.630
and haphazard than we thought.

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:21.080
<i>True...</i>

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:23.480
<i>Animus's power is pretty crazy, too.</i>

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:29.200
By the way, Yako,

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:31.270
you love Amami, don't you?

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:32.270
Huh?

00:10:32.890 --> 00:10:35.480
You fell for him after he saved you, right?

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:40.410
You're not going to confess to him 
while we're here at the beach?

00:10:40.850 --> 00:10:43.530
What does the beach have to do with it?

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:47.410
Apparently, the beach makes people bolder.

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:50.120
Oh, be quiet.

00:10:52.340 --> 00:10:56.340
I get the feeling we can pull this off 
once we understand this random power.

00:10:56.950 --> 00:10:59.680
I won't let Animus destroy it 
with the Biscuit Hammer.

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:03.850
The one to destroy this Earth will be me.

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:06.660
The great Lucifer, Samidare.

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:19.670
Those two... will destroy Earth?

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:20.670
Who?

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:22.060
The Princess?

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:23.950
No, Lucifer?

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:26.410
Sia, we can't...

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:28.130
Yeah, I won't tell anyone.

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:31.120
If the Princess finds out we know, 
they might eliminate us.

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:32.840
No way!

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:37.020
I mean, Amamiya-kun...

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:41.290
He saved me...

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:46.600
Five.

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:47.960
Six.

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:50.190
Then, seven.

00:11:50.190 --> 00:11:51.080
Doubt it!

00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:53.490
You looked!

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:00.100
Four!

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:00.770
Doubt it!

00:12:00.770 --> 00:12:03.370
Oh, come on, again?

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:05.520
Damn it!

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:09.870
It's here?

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:14.730
Everyone, let's go.

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:23.090
It'll be suspicious if you don't come.

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:26.620
Whose side are you on?

00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:29.060
Why haven't you outed me?

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:33.040
I'm not giving you the answers.

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:35.410
Do your homework by yourself.

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:39.530
Who do you think you are?

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:48.780
<i>I'll protect them all!</i>

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:04.710
The one to destroy this Earth will be me.

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:09.000
<i>I have to focus right now.</i>

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:18.610
There it is.

00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:19.980
So that's...

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.340
Seven-eyes.

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:30.640
<i>All our forces united, huh?</i>

00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:33.700
<i>Our Princess's powers have grown, too.</i>

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:36.960
<i>Almost makes me feel bad for the seven-eyes.</i>

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:39.630
Yeah. I can do this.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:41.720
This time I'll crush it!

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:43.550
Here we go!

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:46.250
Hey.

00:13:49.490 --> 00:13:53.100
You combat veterans can sit this one out.

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:55.810
Let's go watch the ocean together.

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:57.600
Amamiya! Asahina!

00:13:58.530 --> 00:14:00.000
You showed yourself, Animus!

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.110
The ocean, right?!

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:03.150
Wait for me, my prey!

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:05.070
Wait! Mikazuki-san!

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:06.770
Huh?!

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:08.820
Forget about him! 
We'll fight with those left here!

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.960
Spread out and distract him!

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:15.740
Look for an opening and strike it!

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:21.710
Whoa, we're floating.

00:14:22.100 --> 00:14:24.920
What is the meaning of this?

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:28.880
Nothing, just a little prank.

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:31.340
A prank?!

00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:34.810
Now, I wonder how many will die.

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:18.350
It's impossible to beat that thing!

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:21.540
It's not agile, but it's not slow either.

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:24.690
The problem is it's constantly moving.

00:15:25.060 --> 00:15:28.460
It's hard to use Holding Fields 
simultaneously on it.

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:32.550
You can just stick them 
to my Inclined Plane.

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:35.020
Though I would like to halt its movements.

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:37.800
It takes three seconds 
to hit it with our spear.

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:40.080
No, we'll want four.

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:44.040
Excuse me.

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:48.000
I'd like to touch it directly, but do you 
think we can make that happen?

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:51.360
You have some plan for after you touch it?

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:54.960
Though...

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:00.140
Then, I'll act as a decoy.

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:03.310
Hanako!

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:05.710
No other choice! Let's go!

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:20.680
No luck?

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:22.500
We're just repeating last time.

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.080
We can't...

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:25.450
...stop it like this.

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:30.550
You were told it's fine 
to defeat it, weren't you?

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:33.300
Pandora doesn't have enough offensive power.

00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:36.640
And my Holding Field's power is average.

00:16:37.110 --> 00:16:39.260
Still, at this rate...

00:16:42.010 --> 00:16:44.390
<i>Golems don't suffer exhaustion.</i>

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:47.860
<i>We'll each get killed 
as our stamina wears out.</i>

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:49.690
<i>We're heading straight toward...</i>

00:16:52.840 --> 00:16:54.400
<i>...total elimination.</i>

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:01.410
Hmm.

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:02.790
Now that I think about it,

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:06.250
this is the first time we've met 
this time around, isn't it?

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:09.130
It's been a while, Anima,

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:12.670
my little sister.

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:13.880
Sister?!

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:15.230
That's right.

00:17:15.230 --> 00:17:18.610
Anima and I are twins.

00:17:18.610 --> 00:17:19.550
Did she not tell you?

00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:28.060
Anima only gained her powers thanks to me,

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:30.730
yet after turning them against me,

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:33.460
she made up all this stuff 
about Knights and Princesses

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:37.000
and made rules to turn it into a game.

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:38.120
<i>A game?</i>

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:40.860
I don't know what to do with her.

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:44.570
She's using human lives as pawns.

00:17:45.950 --> 00:17:47.560
<i>That's it!</i>

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:52.390
<i>I always wondered why Animus didn't 
just drop the hammer right away.</i>

00:17:53.520 --> 00:17:58.310
<i>So Anima used her power to impose 
rules that keep it from activating?</i>

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:03.220
<i>That's why one of the Knights' duties 
is to protect the Princess,</i>

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:07.410
<i>the Game Master who's enforcing the rules.</i>

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:11.190
Anima, what are you plotting this time?

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:16.000
I heard from Hekatombaion.

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:19.360
You sent a golem flying with your own punch?

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:21.160
That's not like you.

00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:26.450
That's not like who?

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:29.500
Who do you think you've 
been talking to all this time?

00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:30.900
Anima?

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:34.050
I am the great Lucifer, Samidare.

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:37.450
The one who will crush 
that hammer, Earth, all of it!

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:38.900
I'm grateful.

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:43.890
You brought me into this battle and 
gave me the chance to obtain this power.

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:47.870
I also... pity you!

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:49.750
For dragging me into this!

00:18:50.680 --> 00:18:52.060
What?

00:18:52.620 --> 00:18:56.010
First, I'll punish you 
for calling people pawns.

00:18:56.010 --> 00:18:57.030
Yuu-kun, footing!

00:18:57.030 --> 00:18:57.980
As you wish!

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:04.660
Hey, now...

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:06.910
You shouldn't point that at others.

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:08.660
Have you no common sense?

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:10.670
One, two—!

00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:20.680
Wh-What?

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:27.020
You're open.

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:53.650
Combination Field: Flametongue.

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:56.790
It was last-minute, but I'm glad it worked.

00:19:58.320 --> 00:19:59.780
I knew it.

00:19:59.780 --> 00:20:02.520
I thought I saw it devour mine.

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:13.770
Unstoppable Spear!

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:17.650
Let's dog-pile it!

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:19.250
Concentrate your Holding Fields on it!

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:48.040
W-We won.

00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:56.900
Yeah!

00:20:57.400 --> 00:21:00.100
We did it!

00:21:00.100 --> 00:21:01.310
Yay!

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:06.440
Amamiya-kun.

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:32.250
Hey!

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:34.730
Yuu-kun! Princess!

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:36.970
Where's Animus?!

00:21:38.210 --> 00:21:39.470
He got away.

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:41.240
Wha?!

00:21:45.080 --> 00:21:46.950
Then, I'll go back and fight seven-eyes!

00:21:47.900 --> 00:21:49.720
How are things on your end?

00:21:51.280 --> 00:21:52.130
Princess.

00:21:52.130 --> 00:21:53.270
Hm?

00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:54.870
They defeated the seven-eyed one.

00:21:57.090 --> 00:21:58.060
Casualties?

00:21:58.060 --> 00:21:59.810
No casualties.

00:21:59.810 --> 00:22:01.370
Oh! That's great.

00:22:02.740 --> 00:22:04.050
Mikazuki?

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:05.780
Yes. He's here.

00:22:05.780 --> 00:22:08.060
He's on the ground in front of me.

00:22:08.060 --> 00:22:09.340
I-It's over?!

00:22:09.340 --> 00:22:11.220
A message? Sure.

00:22:12.240 --> 00:22:16.270
Mikazuki. He says no dinner 
since you ran from the enemy.

00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:19.680
Sounds like a punishment from an old manga.

00:22:20.270 --> 00:22:24.280
By the way, tonight we're planing 
a seafood feast with spiny lobster!

00:22:24.280 --> 00:22:25.750
S-Spiny lobster?!

00:22:24.610 --> 00:22:25.750
Yay!

00:22:25.750 --> 00:22:26.780
S-So fancy!

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:29.280
Wow, spiny lobster?!

00:22:29.280 --> 00:22:31.240
No dinner...

00:22:31.240 --> 00:22:34.990
Seems light for the sin 
of abandoning friends in battle.

00:22:35.600 --> 00:22:39.000
I don't think he was really 
counting on him from the start.

00:22:40.440 --> 00:22:42.920
You did well, Hekatombaion.

00:22:45.030 --> 00:22:46.690
Spiny lobster...

00:22:47.070 --> 00:22:49.480
Spiny lobster sounds good.

00:22:57.080 --> 00:23:05.230
<i>Looking back to those times, 
I always thought</i>

00:23:05.230 --> 00:23:09.790
<i>It was hard to live life true to myself.</i>

00:23:10.450 --> 00:23:13.520
<i>I recall those times.</i>

00:23:13.520 --> 00:23:17.090
<i>I wanted to forget, 
but now it's different.</i>

00:23:17.090 --> 00:23:22.770
<i>Back then we stared at that same sky.</i>

00:23:23.950 --> 00:23:29.500
<i>I'll never forget you, 
or our endless dreams</i>

00:23:29.500 --> 00:23:36.010
<i>As we gazed at that sky 
after fate brought us together</i>

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:41.460
<i>I dream of us together, 
of those days I remember</i>

00:23:41.460 --> 00:23:43.730
<i>But dreams end and I wake up</i>

00:23:43.730 --> 00:23:48.250
<i>Seeking the future</i>

00:23:49.160 --> 00:23:54.300
<i>I reach for the light,</i>

00:23:55.220 --> 00:24:00.720
<i>Always thinking of you in</i>

00:24:04.340 --> 00:24:13.620
<i>every little thing</i>

00:24:22.480 --> 00:24:26.980
<b>Next Episode:
The Asahina Family</b>
